# C7: a solution that isn't linear in its uncertain input over ±1σ comes from Monte Carlo (with a warning).
# y(4 s) = e^(−4k) with k normal (0.5 ± 0.2)/s is log-normal: mean e^(−2 + 8·0.04) = 0.186 m and standard
# deviation 0.186 m · √(e^0.64 − 1) = 0.176 m; the linear rule would give 0.135 ± 0.108 m. The value shown is the
# solution at the measured k, e^(−2) m = 0.135 m, as for a linear solve (red team 14 #6); the spread is Monte Carlo's
k = 0.5 ± 0.2 1/s
seed(1)
solve y' = -k y with y(0 s) = 1.0 m for t from 0 s to 4 s
print y(4 s)
print abs(value(y(4 s)) / 0.1353 m - 1) < 0.01, abs(uncertainty(y(4 s)) / 0.176 m - 1) < 0.1
print y(4 s) - y(4 s)
print value(y(0 s)), uncertainty(y(0 s))
